From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 07:35:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: take the SIO window
 from t8132-sio.dtsi

The SIO coprocessor window is now 0x8000 in t8132-sio.dtsi itself, so
the J604 board file no longer needs to override it. Keep only the board's
DMA channel count.

The resulting device tree is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi | 7 -------
 1 file changed, 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
index b9db4934d2..39f472f477 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
@@ -1182,14 +1182,7 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
-/*
- * The ASC mailbox sits at coprocessor + 0x8000, so the coprocessor window
- * the driver maps stops there, as on T6030 and T6041 (the J604 ADT's 0x88000
- * covers the mailbox). The driver only uses the CPU control register.
- */
 &sio {
-	reg = <0x3 0xade00000 0x0 0x8000>,
-	      <0x3 0xad850000 0x0 0x4000>;
 	dma-channels = <0x80>;
 };
 
